# Vendored libraries. Every file here is version-pinned (see VENDOR.md) and is
# reached through a URL carrying the release stamp - `?v=<version>`, put there
# by tools/assets.php for everything in the import map and by core/assets.js for
# the grammars, Mermaid and MathJax, whose names are decided at runtime. So a
# different build genuinely arrives at a different URL and this directory may be
# cached for as long as the browser likes.
#
# It did not always work that way, and the difference matters. Before the stamp,
# these paths were constant across releases while their contents were not, and
# `immutable` is honoured through a reload AND a hard reload - so upgrading an
# installation left every returning visitor running the new application against
# the previous release's Vue, marked, DOMPurify and Shiki, with no way to clear
# it short of emptying the browser cache by hand.
#
# The rule is stated for the directory rather than per file because there are
# over four hundred of them once the Shiki grammars are counted. The MIME types
# for .js and .mjs are set by the .htaccess in the root.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
    <FilesMatch "\.(js|mjs)$">
        Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
    </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
